ding":null,"first":"Lina","key":"weisslinapau","last":"Weiss","name":"Weiss, Lina","rank":226,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"120","corresponding":null,"first":"Tricia","key":"wevilltriciapau","last":"Wevill","name":"Wevill, Tricia","rank":227,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"78","corresponding":null,"first":"Sa","key":"xiaosapau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Sa","rank":228,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oscar","key":"záratemartínezoscarpau","last":"Zárate Martínez","name":"Zárate Martínez, Oscar","rank":229,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"zobelmartinpau","last":"Zobel","name":"Zobel, Martin","rank":230,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40175550"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-025-08814-5","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"8064","journal":"Nature","pages":"917-924","paperid":"e1400253","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"641"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001849992"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c3c38f96-79d7-43c5-8528-5daee8718f6d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Global impoverishment of natural vegetation revealed by dark diversity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-807446","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: There remains a substantial unmet need for effective and safe treatments for neuropathic pain. The Neuropathic Pain Special Interest Group aimed to update treatment recommendations, published in 2015, on the basis of new evidence from randomised controlled trials, emerging neuromodulation techniques, and advances in evidence synthesis. METHODS: For this systematic review and meta-analysis, we searched Embase, PubMed, the International Clinical Trials Registry, and ClinicalTrials.gov from data inception for neuromodulation trials and from Jan 1, 2013, for pharmacological interventions until Feb 12, 2024. We included double-blind, randomised, placebo-controlled trials that evaluated pharmacological and neuromodulation treatments administered for at least 3 weeks, or if there was at least 3 weeks of follow-up, and which included at least ten participants per group. Trials included participants of any age with neuropathic pain, defined by the International Association for the Study of Pain. We excluded trials with enriched enrolment randomised withdrawal designs and those with participants with mixed aetiologies (ie, neuropathic and non-neuropathic pain) and conditions such as complex regional pain syndrome, low back pain without radicular pain, fibromyalgia, and idiopathic orofacial pain. We extracted summary data in duplicate from published reports, with discrepancies reconciled by a third independent reviewer on the platform Covidence. The primary efficacy outcome was the proportion of responders (50% or 30% reduction in baseline pain intensity or moderate pain relief). The primary safety outcome was the number of participants who withdrew from the treatment owing to adverse events. We calculated a risk difference for each comparison and did a random-effects meta-analysis. Risk differences were used to calculate the number needed to treat (NNT) and the number needed to harm (NNH) for each treatment. Risk of bias was assessed by use of the Cochrane risk of bias tool 2 and certainty of evidence assessed by use of GRADE. Recommendations were based on evidence of efficacy, adverse events, accessibility, and cost, and feedback from engaged lived experience partners. This study is registered on PROSPERO, CRD42023389375. FINDINGS: We identified 313 trials (284 pharmacological and 29 neuromodulation studies) for inclusion in the meta-analysis. Across all studies, 48 789 adult participants were randomly assigned to trial groups (20 611 female and 25 078 male participants, where sex was reported). Estimates for the primary efficacy and safety outcomes were tricyclic antidepressants (TCAs) NNT=4·6 (95% CI 3·2-7·7), NNH=17·1 (11·4-33·6; moderate certainty of evidence), α2δ-ligands NNT=8·9 (7·4-11·10), NNH=26·2 (20·4-36·5; moderate certainty of evidence), serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake inhibitors (SNRIs) NNT=7·4 (5·6-10·9), NNH=13·9 (10·9-19·0; moderate certainty of evidence), botulinum toxin (BTX-A) NNT=2·7 (1·8-9·61), NNH=216·3 (23·5-∞; moderate certainty of evidence), capsaicin 8% patches NNT=13·2 (7·6-50·8), NNH=1129·3 (135·7-∞; moderate certainty of evidence), opioids NNT=5·9 (4·1-10·7), NNH=15·4 (10·8-24·0; low certainty of evidence), repetitive transcranial magnetic stimulation (rTMS) NNT=4·2 (2·3-28·3), NNH=651·6 (34·7-∞; low certainty of evidence), capsaicin cream NNT=6·1 (3·1-∞), NNH=18·6 (10·6-77·1; very low certainty of evidence), lidocaine 5% plasters NNT=14·5 (7·8-108·2), NNH=178·0 (23·9-∞; very low certainty of evidence). The findings provided the basis for a strong recommendation for use of TCAs, α2δ-ligands, and SNRIs as first-line treatments; a weak recommendation for capsaicin 8% patches, capsaicin cream, and lidocaine 5% plasters as second-line recommendation; and a weak recommendation for BTX-A, rTMS, and opioids as third-line treatments for neuropathic pain. INTERPRETATION: Our results support a revision of the Neuropathic Pain Special Interest Group recommendations for the treatment of neuropathic pain. Treatment outcomes are modest and for some treatments uncertainty remains. Further large placebo-controlled or sham-controlled trials done over clinically relevant timeframes are needed. FUNDING: NeuPSIG and ERA-NET Neuron.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Soliman, Nadia","Moisset, Xavier","Ferraro, Michael C","de Andrade, Daniel Ciampi","Baron, Ralf","Belton, Joletta","Bennett, David L H","Calvo, Margarita","Dougherty, Patrick","Gilron, Ian","Hietaharju, Aki J","Hosomi, Koichi","Kamerman, Peter R","Kemp, Harriet","Enax-Krumova, Elena K","McNicol, Ewan","Price, Theodore J","Raja, Srinivasa N","Rice, Andrew S C","Smith, Blair H","Talkington, Fiona","Truini, Andrea","Vollert, Jan","Attal, Nadine","Finnerup, Nanna B","Haroutounian, Simon"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-803831"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["NeuPSIG Review Update Study Group"],"corresponding_author":["Soliman, Nadia"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Chile","Finland","France","Germany","Italy","Japan","South Africa","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hôpital Ambroise Paré","Imperial College London","Johns Hopkins University","Kiel University","Massachusetts College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences","Neuroscience Research Australia","Osaka University","Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile","Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile","Providence Care Hospital","Queen's University Kingston","Ruhr University Bochum","Tampere University Hospital","The University of Osaka","Universite Paris-Saclay","University Hospital of Ruhr-Universität Bochum","University Hospital of Tampere","University of Clermont Auvergne","University of Dundee","University of Exeter","University of New South Wales","University of Oxford","University of Rome La Sapienza","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Texas at Dallas","University of the Witwatersrand","Université Clermont Auvergne","Université Paris-Saclay","Washington University St. Louis"],"keyword":["Analgesics therapeutic use","Electric Stimulation Therapy methods","Humans","Neuralgia therapy","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Independent Researcher"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pharmacotherapy and non invasive neuromodulation for neuropathic pain a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1474-4422(25)00068-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The full-time salary of NS is funded by the Dr Jennie Gwynn Legacy Fund which was a legacy request made to ASCR. NBF's work is supported by a grant from the Lundbeck Foundation R359-2020-2620. EKE-K holds an endowed professorship funded by German Social Accident Insurance since 2020. The face-to-face study meeting was funded by the Networking Group Call 2022 Chronic Pain of the ERA-NET Neuron. None of the authors received funding from any pharmaceutical company or other agency for the preparation of this article. The corresponding author and all coauthors had full access to all the data in the study and had final responsibility for the decision to submit for publication. We thank Emma Shaw, Imperial College London Library for her expert guidance on the search strategy. We also thank those who contributed to the investigation (screening and data extraction phases): Blanca Penaloza, Macarena Tejos-Bravo, Hayley Leake, Kamal Shah, Rebecca Robertson, Alba Izquierdo Barras, Vinod Mahtani, Omar Abu Summaqa, and Jasleen Sambhi. The study received funding from the NeuPSIG committee to support the salary of a research assistant for 6 months and received funding from ERA-NET Neuron to support a face-to-face meeting. The NeuPSIG committee initiated and participated in the study."],"id":"S02-100.00-803831","identifier":[{"id":"40252663","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105002674478","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ccb3a647-26f9-4488-9d48-a3d56654ad74","au-bce699b4-9ecc-487c-9145-e0879267e469"],"keyword":["Analgesics/therapeutic use","Electric Stimulation Therapy/methods","Humans","Neuralgia/therapy","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CA5969A1F0A866832A56120C4CEE0271"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/776999332/1-s2.0-S1474442225000687-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1474-4422(25)00068-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"université clermont auvergne","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Clermont Auvergne","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"university of clermont auvergne","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Clermont Auvergne","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"neuroscience research australia","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Neuroscience Research Australia","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"au","key":"university of new south wales","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of New South Wales","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","No