{"abstract":"Objectives: Management strategies for small bowel obstruction (SBO) vary from conservative approaches to surgical intervention. A known complication of surgery is the subsequent adhesions that can cause recurrent SBOs, longer hospital stays, and higher treatment costs. Our primary outcome was to identify independent risk factors that are associated with the decision for surgical intervention, and our secondary outcome was to describe characteristics of visits associated with complications. Methods: This study was a single-center, retrospective chart review from a large, urban university hospital. We included adult patients admitted to the emergency department (ED) with the International Classification of Diseases, 10th Rev, codes for small bowel obstruction from June 1, 2017– May 30, 2019. Eligible covariates were demographics, radiological findings, clinical presentation, past medical history, and results of radiologic testing. We identified univariate associations of outcome and then performed a multivariate logistic regression to identify independent associations of each outcome. Finally, a backwards selection was used to determine the final model. We calculated odds ratios (OR) and 95% confidence intervals (CI) along with the area under the curve (AUC), as appropriate. Results: A total of 530 patients met the study criteria; 148 (27.9%) underwent surgery of whom 35 (6.6%) had complications. We identified seven independent associations for the decision of surgery: abdominal distension (OR 0.27, 95% CI 0.10–0.62); gastrografin (OR 0.41, 95% CI 0.20–0.81); previous SBO (OR 0.42, 95% CI 0.26–0.66); higher Charlson Comorbidity Index score (OR 0.87, 95% CI 0.80–0.95); nasogastric decompression (OR 2.04, 95% CI 1.25–3.39), initial systolic blood pressure <100 mm Hg (OR 2.65, 95% CI 1.05–6.53); free fluid or volvulus/closed-loop obstruction on computed tomography (OR 7.95, 95% CI 4.25–15.39), with the AUC for the predictive model equaling 0.73. Conclusion: We identified seven independent associations present in the ED associated with the decision for surgery. These associations are a step toward building better prediction models and improving decision-making in the ED, allowing for a more adequate treatment plan.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Berman, Daniel J.","Mahler, Alexander W.","Burke, Ryan C.","Bennett, Andrew E.","Shapiro, Nathan I.","Bilello, Leslie A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-802353"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Berman, Daniel J."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Emergency Service Hospital","Female","Humans","Intestinal Obstruction surgery","Intestine Small surgery","Male","Middle Aged","Postoperative Complications","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"associations of the need for surgery in emergency department patients with small bowel obstructions","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5811/westjem.18455","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-802353","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11908511","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85215120615","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39918153","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-75f5cf35-1aff-48d4-82bb-40ff1b68d852"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Emergency Service, Hospital","Female","Humans","Intestinal Obstruction/surgery","Intestine, Small/surgery","Male","Middle Aged","Postoperative Complications","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25F60198D5381BF5A34A9C691774FA7D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/283452585/qt42m202fq.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5811/westjem.18455","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"beth israel deaconess medical center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel J.","key":"bermanpau","last":"Berman","name":"Berman, Daniel J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander W.","key":"mahlerpau","last":"Mahler","name":"Mahler, Alexander W.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ryan C.","key":"burkepau","last":"Burke","name":"Burke, Ryan C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew E.","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","name":"Bennett, Andrew E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nathan I.","key":"shapiropau","last":"Shapiro","locid":"6aec77d1-9e4f-4cfd-8b18-004ff8b6e6a9","name":"Shapiro, Nathan I.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leslie A.","key":"bilellopau","last":"Bilello","name":"Bilello, Leslie A.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39918153"],"pub":{"doi":"10.5811/westjem.18455","issn":["1936900X","19369018"],"issn_org":["1936900X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Western Journal of Emergency Medicine","pages":"135-141","publisher":"University of California","status":"p","title":"Western Journal of Emergency Medicine","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215120615"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-75f5cf35-1aff-48d4-82bb-40ff1b68d852"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Associations of the Need for Surgery in Emergency Department Patients with Small Bowel Obstructions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-802353","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aims: To explore associations between the axonal protein neurofilament light chain (NfL) and severity of diabetic polyneuropathy (DPN) and pain. Methods: We performed cross-sectional analysis of a subset of the PiNS/DOLORisk cohort of people with DPN with and without neuropathic pain. Biobank samples were analyzed for serum NfL (s-NfL) using single molecule array. DPN was defined by Toronto criteria for probable or confirmed DPN. Painful DPN (PDPN) was evaluated according to IASP criteria. Measures of DPN severity included clinical DPN scales, quantitative sensory testing (QST) and intraepidermal nerve fiber density (IENFD). Results: Participants with confirmed (N = 172) or probable DPN (N = 29) were included. There was no s-NfL difference between participants with DPN (N = 79, 22.8 ng/L [IQR 17.4; 31.3]) and PDPN (N = 122, 22.2 ng/L [16.0; 34.4]). S-NfL was not associated with pain severity or DPN severity evaluated by clinical DPN scales. Higher s-NfL was associated with lower IENFD (13.6 % [95 % CI 3.1; 22.9], unit = 1 fiber/mm, N = 24) and more pronounced loss of nerve fiber function measured by QST (p-trend = 0.02). Conclusions: Higher s-NfL was associated with nerve fiber dysfunction and loss quantified by QST and IENFD, but not with pain or clinical DPN scales. S-NfL may reflect the severity of nerve fiber damage underlying DPN.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Määttä, Laura L.","Andersen, Signe Toft","Parkner, Tina","Hviid, Claus Vinter Bødker","Witte, Daniel R","John, Jishi","Pascal, Mathilde M.V.","Ferris, Eleanor","Baskozos, Georgios","Ramirez, Juan D.","Tesfaye, Solomon","Shillo, Pallai R.","Rice, Andrew S.C.","Laycock, Helen C.","Jensen, Troels Staehelin","Bennett, David L.","Themistocleous, Andreas C."],"cuid":["S02-088.24-813511"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Määttä, Laura L."],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","John Radcliffe Hospital","Sheffield Teaching Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Diabetic polyneuropathy","Neurofilaments","Neuropathic pain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"serum neurofilament light chain and structural and functional nerve fiber loss in painful and painless diabetic polyneuropathy","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2025.112098","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.24-813511","identifier":[{"id":"40118191","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105000594731","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fa7f39ab-9e5a-4677-9f80-9770ba5d4f11","au-7e10bf66-c80e-4d30-b756-24abe88686e1"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Diabetic polyneuropathy","Neurofilaments","Neuropathic pain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FB9197FB6A16DF4EF0329B0EA16A817"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/783610760/M_tt_et_al._2025_Serum_Neurofilament_Light_Chain_and_Structural_and_Functional_Nerve_Fiber_Loss_in_Painful_and_Painless_Diabetic_Polyneuropathy.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.diabres.2025.112098","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","No