{"abstract":"Motivation and autonomy are fundamental concepts in Human-Computer Interaction (HCI), yet in User Experience (UX) research they have remained surprisingly peripheral. We draw on Self-Determination Theory (SDT) to analyse autonomous and non-autonomous patterns of motivation in 497 interaction experiences. Using latent profile analysis, we identify 5 distinct patterns of motivation in technology use — “motivational profiles” — associated with significant differences in need satisfaction, affect, and usability. Users’ descriptions of these experiences also reveal qualitative differences between profiles: from intentional, purposive engagement, to compulsive use which users themselves consider unhealthy. Our results complicate exclusively positive notions of intrinsic motivation, and clarify how extrinsic motivation can contribute to positive UX. Based on these findings we identify open questions for UX and SDT: addressing “hedonic amotivation” — negative experiences in activities which are intrinsically motivated but not otherwise valued — and “design for internalisation” — scaffolding healthy and sustainable patterns of engagement over time.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bennett, Daniel","Mekler, Elisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759418"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beyond intrinsic motivation the role of autonomous motivation in user experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3689044","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759418","identifier":[{"id":"85209074208","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b6fdf1a4-2663-490f-b428-3b8890a13e98"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FF89C1851445FAEE6F6A1DD5864735A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3689044","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3689044","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","name":"Bennett, Daniel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"meklerpau","last":"Mekler","locid":"cf6cfa0b-e3ac-4164-8de2-b956d8e23825","name":"Mekler, Elisa","orcid":"0000-0003-0076-6703","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3689044","issn":["10730516","15577325"],"issn_org":["10730516"],"issue":"5","journal":"ACM Transactions on Computer-Human Interaction","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Computer-Human Interaction","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209074208"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b6fdf1a4-2663-490f-b428-3b8890a13e98"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Beyond Intrinsic Motivation: The Role of Autonomous Motivation in User Experience","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759418","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Distinguishing benign from malignant pancreaticobiliary disease is challenging because of the absence of reliable biomarkers. Circulating extracellular vesicles (EVs) have emerged as functional mediators between cells. Their cargos, including microRNAs (miRNAs), are increasingly acknowledged as an important source of potential biomarkers. This multicentric, prospective study aimed to establish a diagnostic plasma EV-derived miRNA signature to discriminate pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) from benign pancreaticobiliary disease. Methods: Plasma EVs were isolated using size exclusion chromatography (SEC) and characterised using nanoparticle tracking analysis, electron microscopy and Western blotting. EV-RNAs underwent small RNA sequencing to discover differentially expressed markers for PDAC (n = 10 benign vs. 10 PDAC). Candidate EV-miRNAs were then validated in a cohort of 61 patients (n = 31 benign vs. 30 PDAC) by RT-qPCR. Logistic regression and optimal thresholds (Youden Index) were used to develop an EV-miR-200 family model to detect cancer. This model was tested in an independent cohort of 95 patients (n = 30 benign, 33 PDAC, and 32 cholangiocarcinoma). Results: Small RNA sequencing and RT-qPCR showed that EV-miR-200 family members were significantly overexpressed in PDAC vs. benign disease. Combined expression of the EV-miR-200 family showed an AUC of 0.823. In an independent validation cohort, application of this model showed a sensitivity, specificity and AUC of 100%, 88%, and 0.97, respectively, for diagnosing PDAC. Conclusions: This is the first study to validate plasma EV-miR-200 members as a clinically-useful diagnostic biomarker for PDAC. Further validation in larger cohorts and clinical trials is essential. These findings also suggest the potential utility in monitoring response and/or recurrence. Graphical Abstract: (Figure presented.)","author_count":22,"contributors":["Liu, Daniel S.K.","Puik, Jisce R.","Patel, Bhavik Y.","Venø, Morten T.","Vahabi, Mahrou","Prado, Mireia Mato","Webber, Jason P.","Rees, Eleanor","Upton, Flora M.","Bennett, Kate","Blaker, Catherine","Immordino, Benoit","Comandatore, Annalisa","Morelli, Luca","Sivakumar, Shivan","Swijnenburg, Rutger Jan","Besselink, Marc G.","Jiao, Long R.","Kazemier, Geert","Giovannetti, Elisa","Krell, Jonathan","Frampton, Adam E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752562"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Frampton, Adam E.","Giovannetti, Elisa"],"country":["Italy","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Fondazione Pisana per la Scienza ONLUS","Royal Brompton and Harefield NHS Foundation Trust","Royal Surrey County Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Scuola Superiore Sant’Anna","Swansea University","University College London","University of Amsterdam","University of Birmingham","University of Pisa","VU University Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Extracellular vesicles","MicroRNAs","Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unlocking the diagnostic power of plasma extracellular vesicle mir 000000000200 family in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13046-024-03090-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752562","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11229220","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85197687478","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38978141","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-02a69948-2e36-4b05-97d9-e2e7fc7757ed"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Extracellular vesicles","Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma","microRNAs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A66F8BFCDA10EFED381F070FDE016C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13046-024-03090-z","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"royal brompton and harefield nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Brompton and Harefield NHS Foundation Trust","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"vu university amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"VU University Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"amsterdam umc","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Amsterdam UMC","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"royal surrey county hospital nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Surrey County Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - RNA Biology and Innovation","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - iNano-School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Omiics ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"8",