{"abstract":"The Next-Generation (NG) IEDB Tools website (https://nextgen-tools.iedb.org) provides users with a redesigned interface to many of the algorithms for epitope prediction and analysis that were originally released on the legacy IEDB Tools website. The initial release focuses on consolidation of all tools related to HLA class I epitopes (MHC binding, elution, immunogenicity, and processing), making all of these predictions accessible from a single application and allowing for their simultaneous execution with minimal user inputs. Additionally, the PEPMatch tool for identifying highly similar epitopes in a set of curated proteomes, as well as a tool for epitope clustering, are available on the site. The NG Tools site allows users to build data pipelines by sending the output of one tool as input for the next. Over the next several years, all pre-existing IEDB Tools, and any newly developed tools, will be integrated into this new site. Here we describe the philosophy behind the redesign and demonstrate the utility and productivity enhancements that are enabled by the new interface.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Yan, Zhen","Kim, Kevin","Kim, Haeuk","Ha, Brendan","Gambiez, Anaïs","Bennett, Jason","De Almeida Mendes, Marcus Fabiano","Trevizani, Raphael","Mahita, Jarjapu","Richardson, Eve","Marrama, Daniel","Blazeska, Nina","Koşaloǧlu-Yalçln, Zeynep","Nielsen, Morten","Sette, Alessandro","Peters, Bjoern","Greenbaum, Jason A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-775550"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Greenbaum, Jason A."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","La Jolla Institute for Allergy and Immunology","University of California at San Diego"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"next generation iedb tools a platform for epitope prediction and analysis","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkae407","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["IEDB; CEDAR; National Institutes of Health [75N93019C00001, U24CA248138]. Funding for open access charge: NIH [75N93019C00001]. We wish to thank Dr Joseph L. Gabbard and Dr Ali Haskins Lisle of Usability Engineering Services, LLC for their extensive help and feedback with designing the user interface. IEDB; CEDAR; National Institutes of Health [75N93019C00001, U24CA248138]. Funding for open access charge: NIH [75N93019C00001]."],"id":"S01-000.00-775550","identifier":[{"id":"85197816883","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11223806","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38783079","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-74a8ba3b-d144-445e-bc7b-9022d712b6b3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-85FF15F699C38EF2FA90D5B4C40849F9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkae407","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/379764629/66908aa8141ba714af892994.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"la jolla institute for allergy and immunology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"La Jolla Institute for Allergy and Immunology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Bioinformatics"