{"abstract":"The afterword takes the form of a conversation with Jane Bennett. It explores the methods and connections in Michel Serres’s work in relation to the production of knowledge about humans, nature, and the planet. It concludes that Serres might help start conceiving an anthropology that does not just operate on knowledge frequently marked by power struggles but comprehension. Comprehension allows a novel appreciation in and with bodies of what knowledge might imply and accordingly may allow the reader porously to devise better ways to inhabit the world.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bennett, Jane","Bandak, Andreas","Knight M., Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721099"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johns Hopkins University","University of St Andrews"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"afterword conversations with jane bennett","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-721099","ids":["ku-8f9d9cdb-53ed-404c-9c05-d494c425a61f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-BC4B4F2A4B65548F7093FFD100BB7947"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"johns hopkins university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Johns Hopkins University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of st andrews","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of St Andrews","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jane","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","name":"Bennett, Jane","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas","key":"bandakpau","last":"Bandak","locid":"e358540c-8467-40d4-ae35-b9b52bddfa3a","name":"Bandak, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Daniel","key":"knightmpau","last":"Knight M.","name":"Knight M., Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"bandakpedh","last":"Bandak","name":"Bandak, Andreas","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"mknightpedh","last":"M. Knight","name":"M. Knight, Daniel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1215/9781478059318-015","eisbn":["9781478059318"],"isbn":["9781478030287","9781478026051"],"pages":"273-288","publisher":"Duke University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Anthropological Engagements with Michel Serres","title":"Porous Becomings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8f9d9cdb-53ed-404c-9c05-d494c425a61f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Afterword: Conversations with Jane Bennett","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721099","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Environmental knowledge networks (EKNs) link research collaborators in a common purpose to produce data and knowledge to better understand social-ecological phenomena and address environmental challenges. Over recent years, as scientists have grappled with how to produce data and actionable knowledge for conservation and sustainability, more EKNs have been established. Although each network is founded for its own purposes and maintains its own goals and ways of operating, these networks are generally managed by scientists to produce knowledge to advance science and decision making. In this Insight article, we articulate key qualities and benefits of EKNs and shows how EKNs can address grand challenges that cannot be answered by a single team or institution, create a diverse, vibrant culture of science and community of practice, and provide innovative solutions and knowledge to society. We also discuss challenges of EKN governance, and how challenges may vary with a network’s development. Finally, based on a synthesis of structured discussions about key issues in EKN management, we share recommendations and best practices, emphasizing management practices that are inclusive, reflexive, adaptive, and flexible, so that others may benefit from our experience leading EKNs.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Holzer, Jennifer M.","Awada, Tala","Baird, Julia","Bennett, Elena M.","Borer, Elizabeth T.","Contreras, Rafael Calderon","Groffman, Peter M.","Grove, J. Morgan","Harvey, Blane","Hickey, Gordon M.","Hobbs, Imogen","Humphries, Murray M.","Metzger, Marc J.","Orenstein, Daniel E.","Robinson, Brian E.","Watt, Allan D.","Winkler, Klara J.","Asif, Furqan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762215"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Germany","Israel","Mexico","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brock University","Cary Institute of Ecosystem Studies","City University of New York","Federal Environmental Agency, Germany","McGill University","Technion-Israel Institute of Technology","UK Centre for Ecology & Hydrology","USDA Forest Service","Universidad Autónoma Metropolitana","University of Edinburgh","University of Minnesota Twin Cities","University of Nebraska-Lincoln"],"keyword":["Assessment","Collaboration","Environmental knowledge","Environmental research","Evaluation","Knowledge network","Research collaboration","Research network","Research networks","Social ecological system","Team science","Transdisciplinarity","knowledge and innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"managing environmental knowledge networks to navigate complexity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5751/ES-15493-290404","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["NEKN?is?funded?by the?U.S.?National Science?Foundation (NSF)?and?operated by?one?contractor (Batelle). Red SocioEcos was created in 2014 as a \\u201Cnetwork of networks.\\u201D The original idea was to identify and gather research groups in Mexico with common social-ecological interests and a focus on sustainability research. The proposal was supported by the National Council for Science and Technology, and it provided the means for a first thematic gathering of nearly 80 representatives of the different networks involved in social-ecological and sustainability research, outreach, and teaching. The network was formed in 2004 through funding from the European Union under the Framework Programme 6 as an EU Network of Excellence. When the project ended in 2009, Alternet continued with 22 of the original partners. A Council and Management Board facilitate the activities of Alternet, which has grown to 33 partners from 19 countries. EMB, JMH, and KJW acknowledge the support of the Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council of Canada (NSERC), funding reference number NSERC NETGP 523374-18. Cette recherche a \\u00E9t\\u00E9 financ\\u00E9e par le Conseil de recherches en sciences naturelles et en g\\u00E9nie du Canada (CRSNG), [numero de r\\u00E9f\\u00E9rence CRSNG NETGP 523374-18]. DEO acknowledges support from Horizon 2020 (INFRAIA) grants No 871126 (eLTER PPP) and No 871128 (eLTER PLUS). TA acknowledges support from the LTAR-USDA Network (Award number: 58-3042-9-014). JB\\u2019s participation in this work was supported in part by the Canada Research Chairs program. The workshop participation and the majority of the content contribution by KJW happened while working at McGill University. The results do not represent the official opinion of the German Environment Agency or any other federal government entity."],"id":"S01-000.00-762215","identifier":[{"id":"85207529062","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-41d278eb-c60a-4103-bddc-0847b9464f0c"],"keyword":["Collaboration","Environmental knowledge","Research networks","assessment","convergence science","environmental knowledge networks","environmental research","evaluation","knowledge and innovation","knowledge network","research collaboration","research network","social-ecological system","team science","transdisciplinarity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A60160DD106A7EBE261D1FEFE2A19853"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5751/ES-15493-290404","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/748355465/Managing_environmental_knowledge_networks_to_navigate_complexity_ES-2024-15493.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"brock university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Brock University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of nebraska lincoln","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Nebraska-Lincoln","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"mcgill university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McGill University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of minnesota twin cities","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Minnesota Twin Cities","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"mx","key":"universidad autónoma metropolitana","loc":["Mexico","America, Central","OECD"],"name":"Universidad Autónoma Metropolitana","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"city university of new york","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"City University of New York","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"cary institute of ecosystem studies","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cary Institute of Ecosystem Studies","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"us","key":"usda forest service","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"USDA Forest Service","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"il","key":"technion israel institute of technology","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Technion-Israel Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"gb","key":"uk centre for ecology hydrology","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"UK Centre for Ecology & Hydrology","used":1},{"affno":"12","country":"de","key":"federal environmental agency germany","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Federal Environmental Agency, Germany","used":1},{"affno":"13","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-