{"abstract":"Monitoring the governance and management effectiveness of area-based conservation has long been recognized as an important foundation for achieving national and global biodiversity goals and enabling adaptive management. However, there are still many barriers that prevent conservation actors, including those affected by governance and management systems from implementing conservation activities and programs and from gathering and using data on governance and management to inform decision-making across spatial scales and through time. We explored current and past efforts to assess governance and management effectiveness and barriers actors face in using the resulting data and insights to inform conservation decision-making. To help overcome these barriers, we developed Elinor, a free and open-source monitoring tool that builds on the work of Nobel Prize winner Elinor Ostrom to facilitate the gathering, storing, sharing, analyzing, and use of data on environmental governance and management across spatial scales and for areas under different governance and management types. We consider the process of codesigning and piloting Elinor with conservation scientists and practitioners and the main components of the assessment and online data system. We also consider how Elinor complements existing approaches by addressing governance and management in a single assessment at a high level for different types of area-based conservation, providing flexible options for data collection, and integrating a data system with an assessment that can support data use and sharing across different spatial scales, including global monitoring of the Global Biodiversity Framework. Although challenges will continue, the process of developing Elinor and the tool itself offer tangible solutions to barriers that prevent the systematic collection and use of governance and management data. With broader uptake, Elinor can play a valuable role in enabling more effective, inclusive, and durable area-based conservation.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Mahajan, Shauna L.","Obiene, Samson","Ojwang, Lenice","Olwero, Nasser","Valdivia, Abel","Wosu, Adaoma","Adrid, Emily","Andradi-Brown, Dominic A.","Andriamalala, Gildas","Ban, Natalie C.","Bennett, Nathan J.","Blythe, Jessica","Cheng, Samantha H.","Darling, Emily","De Nardo, Matheus","Drury O'Neill, Elizabeth","Epstein, Graham","Fidler, Robert Y.","Fisher, Kim","Geldmann, Jonas","Gill, David A.","Kroner, Rachel Golden","Gurney, Georgina","Jagadish, Arundhati","Jonas, Harry D.","Lazuardi, Muhammad Erdi","Petersen, Samantha","Ranarivelo, Valencia V.","Rasoloformanana, Lilia","Rasolozaka, Tojo M.","Read, Daniel J.","Mwaiteleke, Elia Sabula","Ahmadia, Gabby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-740047"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Blue Ventures Conservation","Brock University","Conservation International","Duke University","Fauna & Flora International","Florida International University","James Cook University Queensland","Stockholm University","The Landscapes and Livelihoods Group","The Peopled Seas Initiative","University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Victoria BC","University of Waterloo","Wildlife Conservation Society"],"keyword":["Biodiversity","Database","Decision making","Governance","Management effectiveness","Monitoring","area based conservation","biodiversidad"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["World Wide Fund for Nature (WWF)"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introducing elinor for monitoring the governance and management of area based conservation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cobi.14213","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-740047","identifier":[{"id":"85184264976","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37904666","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ef7244ec-387d-4cb9-ab39-fee09e9264a5"],"keyword":["area-based conservation","base de datos","biodiversidad","biodiversity","conservación basada en zonas","database","decision-making","efectividad de la gestión","equitable governance","gobernanza","gobernanza equitativa","governance","management effectiveness","monitoreo","monitoring","toma de decisiones","公平治理","决策","基于区域的保护","数据库","治理","生物多样性","监测","管理有效性"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-631DA8ED4271D00ED5A2E5E825A47CA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cobi.14213","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/389310381/Conservation_Biology_2023_Mahajan_Introducing_Elinor_for_monitoring_the_governance_and_management_of_area_based.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["World Wide Fund for Nature (WWF)"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"fauna flora international","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Fauna & Flora International","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"the landscapes and livelihoods group","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Landscapes and Livelihoods Group","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],