o M.","key":"rasolozakapau","last":"Rasolozaka","name":"Rasolozaka, Tojo M.","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel J.","key":"readpau","last":"Read","name":"Read, Daniel J.","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elia Sabula","key":"mwaitelekepau","last":"Mwaiteleke","name":"Mwaiteleke, Elia Sabula","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gabby","key":"ahmadiapau","last":"Ahmadia","name":"Ahmadia, Gabby","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37904666"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cobi.14213","issn":["08888892","15231739"],"issn_org":["08888892"],"issue":"2","journal":"Conservation Biology","paperid":"e14213","status":"p","title":"Conservation Biology","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184264976"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ef7244ec-387d-4cb9-ab39-fee09e9264a5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introducing Elinor for monitoring the governance and management of area-based conservation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-740047","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Thermal-afective experience is a growing topic in Human-Computer Interaction. However, research linking thermal and afective experience in technology use has not moved beyond attempts to establish broad, sweeping associations, such as between warmth and positive afect. One of the obstacles to progression is the need for frameworks and vocabularies that describe and conceptualise the richness of thermal perception and afective experience. To help conceptualise associations between thermal perception and afective experience we turn to Cí poetry, a form of classical Chinese literature rich with evocative descriptions of embodied, environmentally situated, frst-person experience. We conducted a lexical analysis to identify thermal-afective associations, and propose a design framework addressing thermal design. We demonstrate the value of this framework via analysis of existing thermal design exemplars.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Feng, Feng","Bennett, Daniel","Mekler, Elisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747222"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross cultural","Design","Emotion","Framework","Lexicon","Multisensory","Thermal","Translation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"smiles summon the warmth of spring a framework for thermal and affective design grounded in classical chinese poetry","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661620","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747222","identifier":[{"id":"85200394791","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-442081bc-5047-4a4b-be67-b4a24760e2a7"],"keyword":["Thermal","afect","cross-cultural","design","emotion","framework","lexicon","multisensory","translation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3D6CA289F151D89FE0F8FB4B4CEACE54"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661620","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3643834.3661620","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Feng","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","locid":"dac0e506-da5d-4ee6-8783-5abd2a2096f3","name":"Feng, Feng","orcid":"0000-0002-7127-5437","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","name":"Bennett, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"meklerpau","last":"Mekler","locid":"cf6cfa0b-e3ac-4164-8de2-b956d8e23825","name":"Mekler, Elisa","orcid":"0000-0003-0076-6703","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3661620","isbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"2802-2819","status":"p","title":"DIS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200394791"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-442081bc-5047-4a4b-be67-b4a24760e2a7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Smiles Summon the Warmth of Spring: A Framework for Thermal and Affective Design Grounded in Classical Chinese Poetry","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747222","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND. In type 1 diabetes (T1D), impaired insulin sensitivity may contribute to the development of diabetic kidney disease (DKD) through alterations in kidney oxidative metabolism. METHODS. Young adults with T1D (n = 30) and healthy controls (HCs) (n = 20) underwent hyperinsulinemic-euglycemic clamp studies, MRI, 11C-acetate PET, kidney biopsies, single-cell RNA-Seq, and spatial metabolomics to assess this relationship. RESULTS. Participants with T1D had significantly higher glomerular basement membrane (GBM) thickness compared with HCs. T1D participants exhibited lower insulin sensitivity and cortical oxidative metabolism, correlating with higher insulin sensitivity. Proximal tubular transcripts of TCA cycle and oxidative phosphorylation enzymes were lower in T1D. Spatial metabolomics showed reductions in tubular TCA cycle intermediates, indicating mitochondrial dysfunction. The Slingshot algorithm identified a lineage of proximal tubular cells progressing from stable to adaptive/maladaptive subtypes, using pseudotime trajectory analysis, which computationally orders cells along a continuum of states. This analysis revealed distinct distribution patterns between T1D and HCs, with attenuated oxidative metabolism in T1D attributed to a greater proportion of adaptive/maladaptive subtypes with low expression of TCA cycle and oxidative phosphorylation transcripts. Pseudotime progression associated with higher HbA1c, BMI, and GBM, and lower insulin sensitivity and cortical oxidative metabolism. CONCLUSION. These early structural and metabolic changes in T1D kidneys may precede clinical DKD.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Choi, Ye Ji","Richard, Gabriel","Zhang, Guanshi","Hodgin, Jeffrey B.","Demeke, Dawit S.","Yang, Yingbao","Schaub, Jennifer A.","Tamayo, Ian M.","Gurung, Bhupendra K.","Naik, Abhijit S.","Nair, Viji","Birznieks, Carissa","MacDonald, Alexis","Narongkiatikhun, Phoom","Gross, Susan","Driscoll, Lynette","Flynn, Maureen","Tommerdahl, Kalie","Nadeau, Kristen J.","Shah, Viral N.","Vigers, Tim","Snell-Bergeon, Janet K.","Kendrick, Jessica","van Raalte, Daniel H.","Li, Lu Ping","Prasad, Pottumarthi","Ladd, Patricia","Chin, Bennett B.","Cherney, David Z.","McCown, Phillip J.","Alakwaa, Fadhl","Otto, Edgar A.","Brosius, Frank C.","Saulnier, Pierre Jean","Puelles, Victor G.","Goodrich, Jesse A.","Street, Kelly","Venkatachalam, Manjeri A.","Ruiz, Aaron","de Boer, Ian H.","Nelson, Robert G.","Pyle, Laura","Blondin, Denis P.","Sharma, Kumar","Kretzler, Matthias","Bjornstad, Petter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786984"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bjornstad, Petter"],"country":["Canada","France","Germany","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Natera, Inc","Universite de Poitiers","Universite de Sherbrooke","University of Amsterdam","University of Arizona","University of Chicago","University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus","University of Colorado Denver","University of Hamburg","University of Michigan","University of Southern California","University of Texas at San Antonio","University of Toronto","University of Washington"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attenuated kidney oxidative metabolism in young adults with type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI183984","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-786984","identifier":[{"id":"39436695","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85212271634","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11645151","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-33c0c145-77a1-4978-94fc-26ee1fe491e8"],"lang":"English","level"