d","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052313120"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1a40647c-e39c-440f-ad98-062eed962229"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The GAGOme : a cell-based library of displayed glycosaminoglycans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-409103","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Procrastination can be stressful and frustrating, but it seldom causes any major distress. However, for some people, it can become problematic, resulting in anxiety, lowered mood, physical complaints, and decreased well-being. Still, few studies have investigated the benefits of targeting procrastination. In addition, no attempt has previously been made to determine the overall efficacy of providing psychological treatments.Methods: A systematic review and meta-analysis was conducted by searching for eligible records in Scopus, Proquest, and Google Scholar. Only randomized controlled trials comparing psychological treatments for procrastination to an inactive comparator and assessing the outcomes by a self-report measure were included. A random effects model was used to determine the standardized mean difference Hedge's g at post-treatment. Furthermore, test for heterogeneity was performed, fail-safe N was calculated, and the risk of bias was explored. The study was pre-registered at Prospero: CRD42017069981.Results: A total of 1,639 records were identified, with 12 studies (21 comparisons, N = 718) being included in the quantitative synthesis. Overall effect size g when comparing treatment to control was 0.34, 95% Confidence Interval [0.11, 0.56], but revealing significant heterogeneity, Q(20) = 46.99, p < 0.00, and I2 = 61.14%, 95% CI [32.83, 84.24]. Conducting a subgroup analysis of three out of four studies using cognitive behavior therapy (CBT) found an effect size g of 0.55, 95% CI [0.32, 0.77], and no longer showing any heterogeneity, Q(4) = 3.92, p = 0.42, I2 = 0.00%, 95% CI [0.00, 91.02] (N = 236). Risk of publication bias, as assessed by the Egger's test was not significant, z = −1.05, p = 0.30, fail-safe N was 370 studies, and there was some risk of bias as rated by two independent researchers. In terms of secondary outcomes, the self-report measures were too varied to present an aggregated estimate.Conclusions: Psychological treatments seem to have small benefits on procrastination, but the studies displayed significant between-study variation. Meanwhile, CBT was associated with a moderate benefit, but consisted of only three studies. Recommendations for future research are provided, including the use of more valid and reliable outcomes and a screening interview at intake.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rozental, Alexander","Bennett, Sophie","Forsström, David","Ebert, David Daniel","Shafran, Roz","Andersson, Gerhard","Carlbring, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-613558"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","Linköping University","Stockholm University","University College London","University of Erlangen-Nuremberg, Germany"],"keyword":["Cognitive behavior therapy","Meta analysis","Procrastination","Psychological treatments","Systematic review"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeting procrastination using psychological treatments a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2018.01588","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-613558","identifier":[{"id":"85052805288","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30214421","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6125391","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-8cdca752-0a78-4673-84df-4c192f1bf06e"],"keyword":["Cognitive behavior therapy","Meta-analysis","Procrastination","Psychological treatments","Systematic review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3491BD043BB835970E41C4CD7EAE8C6B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/142838175/fpsyg_09_01588.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2018.01588","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karolinska institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of erlangen nuremberg germany","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Erlangen-Nuremberg, Germany","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"linköping university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linköping University","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, INSIDE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"rozentalpau","last":"Rozental","name":"Rozental, Alexander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sophie","key":"bennettpau","last":"Bennett","name":"Bennett, Sophie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"forsströmpau