 P.","key":"conomosmatthewppau","last":"Conomos","name":"Conomos, Matthew P.","rank":67,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Patrick","key":"heagertypatrickpau","last":"Heagerty","name":"Heagerty, Patrick","rank":68,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Teri","key":"manolioteripau","last":"Manolio","name":"Manolio, Teri","rank":69,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17","first":"Louis R.","key":"pasqualelouisrpau","last":"Pasquale","name":"Pasquale, Louis R.","rank":70,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Christopher A.","key":"haimanchristopherapau","last":"Haiman","name":"Haiman, Christopher A.","rank":71,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Neil","key":"caporasoneilpau","last":"Caporaso","name":"Caporaso, Neil","rank":72,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bruce S.","key":"weirbrucespau","last":"Weir","name":"Weir, Bruce S.","rank":73,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22561516"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ng.2271","issn":["10614036","15461718"],"issn_org":["10614036"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"642-650","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861591789"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-59332eba-ce86-497e-a8f6-3c532507c32a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Detectable clonal mosaicism from birth to old age and its relationship to cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446801","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Menkes Disease (MD) is a rare X-linked recessive fatal neurodegenerative disorder caused by mutations in the ATP7A gene, and most patients are males. Female carriers are mosaics of wild-type and mutant cells due to the random X inactivation, and they are rarely affected. In the largest cohort of MD patients reported so far which consists of 517 families we identified 9 neurologically affected carriers with normal karyotypes.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Møller, Lisbeth Birk","Lenartowicz, Malgorzata","Zabot, Marie-Therese","Josiane, Arnaud","Burglen, Lydie","Bennett, Chris","Riconda, Daniel","Fisher, Richard","Janssens, Sandra","Mohammed, Shehla","Ausems, Margreet","Tümer, Zeynep","Horn, Nina","Jensen, Thomas G."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-021206"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adenosine Triphosphatases","Cation Transport Proteins","Chromosomes Human X","Copper","Female","Gene Expression Regulation","Humans","Karyotype","Male","Menkes Kinky Hair Syndrome","Mutation","Phenotype"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical expression of menkes disease in females with normal karyotype","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1750-1172-7-6","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-021206","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3298521","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84858159382","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22264391","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-74bb4068-8e28-4faf-96ce-b68986288841","ku-fba775a6-3379-42c2-b17c-9191ce35378b"],"keyword":["Adenosine Triphosphatases","Cation Transport Proteins","Chromosomes, Hu